== Appendix I. AP-S requirement checklist

Every item is unchecked on 2026-10-04; each depends on reading the official call in full first.

- #sym.ballot official call read in full and Part IX corrected against it
- #sym.ballot decision recorded to pursue the contest, with scope
- #sym.ballot team of 2 to 5 students, at least half undergraduates by end of May 2027
- #sym.ballot AP-S member mentor, letter agreeing to supervise and advance costs
- #sym.ballot receive only compliance confirmed for the chosen receiver
- #sym.ballot COTS transmitters chosen, certified for use in Japan
- #sym.ballot communication mode: N = 4 feasibility gate written and run
- #sym.ballot receiver able to separate wanted and interfering sources chosen
- #sym.ballot sensing task chosen, simplest reproducible first
- #sym.ballot real time dashboard designed
- #sym.ballot whole system bill of materials under US\$1,500
- #sym.ballot four page proposal, 12 point Times New Roman, by 31 December 2026 (GMT-10)
- #sym.ballot if selected: video, replication instructions and five page report by 24 May 2027
